cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it and the accompanying manuscript once it is public."
title: "ratio-closure-simplex: a primal and dual simplex specialised to maximum-ratio closure and its canonical decomposition"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Furini
    given-names: Fabio
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/fabiofurini/ratio-closure-simplex"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-09-06"
abstract: >
  C++20 implementation of the ratio-closure simplex: the ordinary primal and
  dual simplex specialised to the normalised maximum-ratio closure linear
  program on an arbitrary precedence DAG, used to produce the entire canonical
  sequence of closure layers and not only the maximum-ratio one. Ships two
  independent certified reference backends (Dinkelbach with minimum cuts, and a
  parametric divide-and-conquer decomposition), an exhaustive rational oracle,
  a synthetic instance generator, frozen data splits, a reproducible campaign
  runner and the experimental report generated from the stored campaigns.
keywords:
  - maximum closure
  - fractional programming
  - network simplex
  - precedence constraints
  - parametric optimisation
